IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 7 (industrial injuries benefits), Part II (disablement gratuity, paragraph 9) and Part III (increase of disablement pension
-- during hospital treatment, paragraph 10). The converter dropped the paragraph numbers; 9 and 10 follow the in-text citations
-- ("paragraph 9(3) of that Schedule" at src:5355; "paragraph 11(10)" for Part IV; "paragraph 15", "paragraph 16" and "paragraph 18" for Part VI).
-- Inputs named `sch 6 ...` and `sch 4 pt V ...` are other provisions' answers, taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 5, seams S21 and S34).

§ `Schedule 7 Part II -- disablement gratuity`

-- 9(3): a person is not entitled to disablement gratuity until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays)
-- beginning with the day of the relevant accident. This counts the days: Sundays are skipped (daydate's Sunday is 0), and the result
-- is the day after the 90th day that is not a Sunday.
-- src:5468 | (3) A person shall not be entitled to disablement gratuity until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident.
@ref sch 7 pt II para 9(3) (src:5468)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the days still to count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the day after counting` MEANS
    IF `the days still to count` AT MOST 0
    THEN day
    ELSE IF ((Day day) MODULO 7) EQUALS 0
         THEN `sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the day after counting` (day PLUS 1) `the days still to count`
         ELSE `sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the day after counting` (day PLUS 1) (`the days still to count` MINUS 1)

-- src:5468 | (3) A person shall not be entitled to disablement gratuity until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident.
@ref sch 7 pt II para 9(3) (src:5468)
GIVEN `the day of the relevant accident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the first day after the 90 days` MEANS
    `sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the day after counting` `the day of the relevant accident` 90

-- src:5468 | (3) A person shall not be entitled to disablement gratuity until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident.
@ref sch 7 pt II para 9(3) (src:5468)
GIVEN `the day of the relevant accident` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the person may be entitled to a gratuity on the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the first day after the 90 days` `the day of the relevant accident`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person shall not be entitled to disablement gratuity until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "until after the expiry": after the 90 days the sub-paragraph says nothing; sub-paragraph (1) decides

-- 9(1): an employed earner is entitled to a disablement gratuity if (a) a claim for disablement benefit was made before 1 October 1986,
-- (b) the loss of faculty from the relevant accident is assessed under Schedule 6 at not less than 1 per cent and (c) the extent is assessed
-- for the period taken into account at less than 20 per cent. The assessed extent is Schedule 6's answer (seam S21), taken as an input.
-- src:5461 | (1) An employed earner shall be entitled to a disablement gratuity, if—
-- src:5462 | (a) he made a claim for disablement benefit before 1st October 1986;
-- src:5463 | (b) he suffered as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty such that the extent of the resulting disablement assessed in accordance with Schedule 6 to this Act amounts to not less than 1 per cent.; and
-- src:5464 | (c) the extent of the disablement is assessed for the period taken into account as amounting to less than 20 per cent.
@ref sch 7 pt II para 9(1) (src:5461-5464)
GIVEN `the person is an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claim for disablement benefit was made` IS A DATE
      `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt II para 9(1) the employed earner is entitled to a disablement gratuity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the extent of disablement is Schedule 6's answer and none has been given
    WHEN JUST extent THEN
        IF `the person is an employed earner` AND (`the day the claim for disablement benefit was made` LESS THAN Date 1 10 1986) AND (extent AT LEAST 1) AND (extent LESS THAN 20)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be entitled to a disablement gratuity, if— (a) he made a claim for disablement benefit before 1st October 1986; (b) ... not less than 1 per cent.; and (c) ... less than 20 per cent."

-- 9(2)(a): the gratuity is of an amount fixed by a prescribed scale, by the length of the period and the degree of disablement, but not
-- in any case exceeding the amount specified in Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 9 (omitted from this text, so an input).
-- src:5465 | (2) A disablement gratuity shall be—
-- src:5466 | (a) of an amount fixed, in accordance with the length of the period and the degree of the disablement, by a prescribed scale, but not in any case exceeding the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 9; and
@ref sch 7 pt II para 9(2)(a) (src:5465-5466)
GIVEN `the amount fixed by the prescribed scale for the length of the period and the degree of disablement` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 9 the maximum disablement gratuity in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt II para 9(2)(a) the amount of the gratuity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount fixed by the prescribed scale for the length of the period and the degree of disablement`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the scale is prescribed by regulations
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 9 the maximum disablement gratuity in pounds`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the table in Schedule 4 is omitted from this text
        WHEN JUST cap THEN JUST (min fixed cap)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not in any case exceeding the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 9"

-- 9(2)(b): payable by instalments if and in such cases as regulations so provide.
-- src:5467 | (b) payable, if and in such cases as regulations so provide, by instalments.
@ref sch 7 pt II para 9(2)(b) (src:5467)
GIVEN `regulations provide that the gratuity is payable by instalments in the case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt II para 9(2)(b) the gratuity is payable by instalments` MEANS
    `regulations provide that the gratuity is payable by instalments in the case`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "if and in such cases as regulations so provide"

§ `Schedule 7 Part III -- increase of disablement pension during hospital treatment`

-- 10(1): this Part has effect in relation to a period of in-patient treatment in a hospital or similar institution which (a) commenced before
-- 6 April 1987, or (b) commenced after that date but within 28 days from the end of the period during which the person last received an
-- increase of benefit under section 62 of the 1975 Act or this paragraph in respect of such treatment for the relevant injury or loss of faculty.
-- src:5470 | (1) This Part of this Schedule has effect in relation to a period during which a person is receiving medical treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution and which—
-- src:5471 | (a) commenced before 6th April 1987; or
-- src:5472 | (b) commenced after that date but within a period of 28 days from the end of the period during which he last received an increase of benefit under section 62 of the 1975 Act or this paragraph in respect of such treatment for the relevant injury or loss of faculty.
@ref sch 7 pt III para 10(1) (src:5470-5472)
GIVEN `the period is one during which the person is receiving medical treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the period commenced` IS A DATE
      `the end of the period during which the person last received an increase of benefit in respect of such treatment for the relevant injury or loss of faculty` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt III para 10(1) this Part has effect in relation to the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the period is one during which the person is receiving medical treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a period during which a person is receiving medical treatment as an in-patient"
        IF `the day the period commenced` LESS THAN Date 6 4 1987 THEN JUST TRUE   -- limb (a)
        IF within28 THEN JUST TRUE   -- limb (b)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither (a) nor (b) is met
    WHERE
        within28 MEANS
            CONSIDER `the end of the period during which the person last received an increase of benefit in respect of such treatment for the relevant injury or loss of faculty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST lastEnd THEN (`the day the period commenced` GREATER THAN Date 5 4 1987) AND (`the day the period commenced` AT MOST (lastEnd PLUS 28))

-- 10(2) and (3): where the extent is assessed for the period at less than 100 per cent it is treated as assessed at 100 per cent for any
-- part of the period during which the person receives in-patient treatment for the relevant injury; but where it is assessed at less than
-- 20 per cent sub-paragraph (2) does not affect the assessment.
-- src:5473 | (2) Where a person is awarded disablement benefit, but the extent of his disablement is assessed for the period taken into account by the assessment at less than 100 per cent., it shall be treated as assessed at 100 per cent. for any part of that period, whether before or after the making of the assessment or the award of benefit, during which he receives, as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution, medical treatment for the relevant injury or loss of faculty.
-- src:5474 | (3) Where the extent of the disablement is assessed for that period at less than 20 per cent., sub-paragraph (2) above shall not affect the assessment; but in the case of a disablement pension payable by virtue of this paragraph to a person awarded a disablement gratuity wholly or partly in respect of the same period, the weekly rate of the pension (after allowing for any increase under Part V of this Act) shall be reduced by the amount prescribed as being the weekly value of his gratuity.
@ref sch 7 pt III para 10(2) and (3) (src:5473-5474)
GIVEN `the extent assessed for the period taken into account, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the person receives medical treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution for the relevant injury or loss of faculty during the part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt III para 10(2) the extent treated as assessed for the part of the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the extent assessed for the period taken into account, as a percentage` LESS THAN 20
            THEN JUST `the extent assessed for the period taken into account, as a percentage`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sub-paragraph (2) above shall not affect the assessment"
        IF `the person receives medical treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution for the relevant injury or loss of faculty during the part of the period` AND (`the extent assessed for the period taken into account, as a percentage` LESS THAN 100)
            THEN JUST 100
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is awarded disablement benefit, but the extent ... at less than 100 per cent": otherwise the assessment stands and sub-paragraph (2) says nothing

-- 10(3), second limb: the weekly rate of a disablement pension payable by virtue of this paragraph to a person awarded a gratuity
-- wholly or partly in respect of the same period is reduced (after allowing for any increase under Part V of this Act) by the amount
-- prescribed as the weekly value of the gratuity.
-- src:5474 | (3) Where the extent of the disablement is assessed for that period at less than 20 per cent., sub-paragraph (2) above shall not affect the assessment; but in the case of a disablement pension payable by virtue of this paragraph to a person awarded a disablement gratuity wholly or partly in respect of the same period, the weekly rate of the pension (after allowing for any increase under Part V of this Act) shall be reduced by the amount prescribed as being the weekly value of his gratuity.
@ref sch 7 pt III para 10(3) (src:5474)
GIVEN `the disablement pension is payable by virtue of this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was awarded a disablement gratuity wholly or partly in respect of the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the pension after allowing for any increase under Part V` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed as the weekly value of the gratuity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 7 pt III para 10(3) the weekly rate of the pension after the reduction` MEANS
    IF `the disablement pension is payable by virtue of this paragraph` AND `the person was awarded a disablement gratuity wholly or partly in respect of the same period`
    THEN `the weekly rate of the pension after allowing for any increase under Part V` MINUS `the amount prescribed as the weekly value of the gratuity`   -- the reduction the sub-paragraph requires
    ELSE `the weekly rate of the pension after allowing for any increase under Part V`
